Local patches to the bundled hiredis, applied by Makefile.PL before the
build. The deps/hiredis submodule stays pristine upstream: never edit it in
place, refresh this file instead. After updating the submodule, check that
this still applies and still covers every server-reachable abort or
over-read (t/protocol_violation.t exercises them). Bump the /N revision in
every marker when changing this file: a worktree holding an older revision
then fails loudly instead of building stale.

A hostile server must fail the connection with a protocol error, not abort
the process or misroute replies: unsolicited replies on a connection that
is not subscribed, malformed pub/sub messages and attributes inside an
aggregate disconnect with REDIS_ERR_PROTOCOL instead of tripping assert(),
over-reading the reply or handing an element to the next callback. An
attribute ahead of a reply is dropped so that reply arrives intact.

A free requested inside a push callback is honoured before pending command
replies are awaited, just as it is after an ordinary reply callback.

